      "math_academy_id": "q-224481",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(11)$ given below, compute $P(X<10).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1432\\,$ | $\\,0.2320\\,$ | $\\,0.3405\\,$ | $\\,0.4599\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.6887\\,$ | $\\,0.7813\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<10) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,9\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 9) \\\\  & =F(9) \\\\  & =0.3405.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
